{
  "cell": "ro_array_core",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md's",
    "'Composing a gate' section for the shared floorplan reasoning, and",
    "layout/ro_array_core/README.md for this cell's own result. This is the",
    "promotion of layout/ro_array_core-placement-poc/ (nine hand-maintained",
    "gen-compose requests, no --check reproducibility) into one recipe.",
    "",
    "ro_array_core is design/ro_array_core.spice's whole entropy source: four",
    "DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT ro_ring5 rings (wstv 0.42/0.44/0.46/0.48, four",
    "physically distinct committed cells -- DR-0003 s8's decorrelation intent),",
    "four ro_buf output buffers, and a three-xor2 combining tree",
    "(xa1=xor(ro1,ro2), xa2=xor(ro3,ro4), xa3=xor(t1,t2)=xo). 132 devices.",
    "",
    "SIX STAGES, and why the PoC's nine requests collapse to six.",
    "The PoC's signal..signal6 were not a chain: each re-composed the SAME",
    "eleven-block floorplan from the leaf cells with one more net routed than",
    "the last, so only the last of them (signal6) is load-bearing -- the five",
    "before it are increment history, kept there, not recipe. signal7..signal9",
    "ARE a chain (each places the previous stage's own GDS as one block), and",
    "become stages 2-4 here. Stages 5-6 are new (the vss taps).",
    "",
    "1. 'core' -- the eleven-block floorplan plus every li1-pin-reachable",
    "   signal net on metal2 (met1): rn1-rn4 (ring.ro -> buf.a), ro1-ro4",
    "   (buf.y -> xa1/xa2 a/b), the four-buffer vss bus, t1 (xa1.y -> xa3.a),",
    "   and t2/b3, the two met1 promotion STUBS t2's met2 bridge needs. en1-en4,",
    "   vddr1-vddr4 and xo are exposed as bare pins straight off each ring's /",
    "   xa3's own already-formed internal node.",
    "2. 't2bridge' -- t2 (xa2.y -> xa3.b) really routed on metal3 (met2) at",
    "   y = 31.0, over the top of row 2. Needs stage 1's two met1 stubs first:",
    "   met2's via-drop is single-hop-only and cannot reach a bare li1 pin.",
    "3. 'vddstub' -- seven metal2 (met1) promotion stubs, one per ro_buf/xor2",
    "   vdd tap. vdd ties to each instance's own nwell, and nwell has no",
    "   chip-wide identity the way the p-substrate does, so these seven really",
    "   are seven separate nets until stage 4 straps them.",
    "4. 'vddbus' -- the six-leg metal3 (met2) vdd bus. SIX two-pin legs, not",
    "   one seven-pin net: waypoints_um is only accepted for a two-pin net, and",
    "   gen-compose rejects a leg crossing an already-accepted leg unless the",
    "   two share a pin -- so the legs form a CHAIN, buf4-buf3-buf2-buf1-xa1-",
    "   xa2-xa3. Row-1 lane y = 7.5 (1.2um above every ring's own upper met2",
    "   rail); xa1->xa2 hops over the top at y = 28.9 and xa2->xa3 drops under",
    "   at y = 10.5, both dodging t2's own y = 31.0 bridge.",
    "5. 'vssstub' -- three metal2 (met1) promotion stubs, one per xor2 vss tap",
    "   (pst's own TAP_S, block-local (3.92, -1.29)). The tips are NOT all at",
    "   one y: ro4's own met1 backbone runs at y = 10.0 across x in [49.5,",
    "   216.4], directly under xa3 but not under xa1/xa2, so xa3's stub stops",
    "   at y = 10.8 while xa1/xa2's reach y = 9.6. Measured before drawn --",
    "   see vss-tap-scan.py, and layout/README.md on why klt drc clean is not",
    "   connectivity evidence for a stub that starts inside a placed block.",
    "6. 'vssbus' (final) -- the array-wide vss strap on metal3 (met2). The four",
    "   rings need NO stub: each already carries its own full-width met2 vss",
    "   rail at y = -3.0 (layout/ro_ring5/'s fourth stage), and the four rails",
    "   are collinear, so three legs in the inter-ring gaps chain them. One",
    "   0.425um leg drops onto the four-buffer vss met1 bus at (57.99, -3.425).",
    "   Reaching row 2 has exactly two doors: the stage-4 vdd bus occupies",
    "   y = 7.5 across x in [5.765, 212.995] and met2 cannot cross met2, so the",
    "   riser goes up at x = 214.5 (east of the vdd bus's own end) and runs back",
    "   west at y = 10.8 to xa3, then 66.0/9.6 down to xa2 and xa1.",
    "",
    "NOT LVS-BLOCKING, AND DRAWN ANYWAY (stages 5-6): klt extract's sky130 deck",
    "ties every un-isolated NMOS body to one global substrate node, so vss was",
    "already one 122-device net before any of this metal existed (DR-0005",
    "finding 3, confirmed at array level by the PoC's Increment 5). net_count",
    "is 96 with and without stages 5-6. A fabricated die still needs the",
    "explicit low-impedance strap the substrate's own unmodelled resistance",
    "does not provide, which is what these two stages draw.",
    "",
    "THE LVS REFERENCE. design/ro_array_core.spice defines ONE .subckt",
    "ro_ring5 and calls it four times with four different wstv overrides, while",
    "layout/ holds four physically distinct ring cells -- so lvs.dependencies'",
    "single shared params dict cannot express it. lvs.dependency_variants below",
    "is compose-cell.py's generic answer (#70): one renamed, separately",
    "parametrized copy of ro_ring5 plus its own nested ro_nand2/ro_stage per",
    "ring (_r1.._r4), with the top subckt's xr1-xr4 instance lines repointed at",
    "them. The renames exist ONLY inside the generated reference (so",
    "flatten_reference has four distinct definitions to inline); nothing in",
    "design/ or in the layout is renamed. lvs-negative-controls.py proves the",
    "resulting match is discriminating rather than vacuous."
  ],
